C. INTERSTATE COMMERCE ELEMENT
- Hawai'i courts enforcing custody across state lines (federal question)
- Child support payments cross state boundaries (commerce clause)
- DHS contracted with federal-funded agencies

**§ 1201 jurisdiction satisfied.**

II. STATUTORY ELEMENTS — 18 U.S.C. § 1201

**Kidnapping requires:**
1. ✓ Unlawful seizing/confining of person (child removed from custody)
2. ✓ Without legal justification (judgment based on unsubstantiated allegations)
3. ✓ Intent to hold for ransom/reward/other purpose (DHS payment structure incentivizes findings)
4. ✓ Movement across state lines OR use of interstate facilities (Hawai'i jurisdiction)

**All elements present.**

**Penalties: Up to life imprisonment; $250,000 fine**

